Base used as a value instead of a member-access head (diag.base_standalone,
error, in and out of class context alike). Near misses in the same class:
Base:Init() (well formed, :INHERIT present) and oUri:Base / oUri:Base:Host
(member named Base on another receiver, D10, issue #258).
-- input.ssl --
:CLASS LinkWidget;
:INHERIT Lab.Control;
:DECLARE oParent;

:PROCEDURE Init;
	:PARAMETERS oUri;
	:DECLARE sRoot, sHost;
	Base:Init();
	Me:oParent := Base;
	sRoot := oUri:Base;
	sHost := oUri:Base:Host;
	:RETURN sRoot + sHost;
:ENDPROC;
-- format --
:CLASS LinkWidget;
:INHERIT Lab.Control;
:DECLARE oParent;

:PROCEDURE Init;
	:PARAMETERS oUri;
	:DECLARE sRoot, sHost;

	Base:Init();
	Me:oParent := Base;
	sRoot := oUri:Base;
	sHost := oUri:Base:Host;

	:RETURN sRoot + sHost;
:ENDPROC;
-- diagnostics --
9:16-9:20 error base_standalone: 'Base' must be used as 'Base:MemberName' and cannot stand alone
-- diagnostics [--strict --info] --
9:16-9:20 error base_standalone: 'Base' must be used as 'Base:MemberName' and cannot stand alone
